<<~ ahu #/law>>

! The One-Hull Law — Island Isomorphism

''Islands differ by grant, never by hull.''

Every wiki island — `lares`-as-wiki, any content wiki, and ''`@daemon` itself'' — MUST comprise the same isomorphic stack: the keel's manifest handshake, capability grants, CRDT sync ports, the `ea` breath declaration, the same worker lifecycle, the same protocol surface. Like the turn-exchange chiasmus, one frame carries every exchange; what a turn //may do// rides its content, never a different frame.

`@daemon` differs ONLY by its endowment: additional capability grants for managing the island mesh internally (mount/evict/residency policy) and mesh connections externally (relay, federation edges). The ocap powerbox names this shape: a normal object holding extraordinary grants. Authority = designation + permission, never architecture.

''The hole this law names (drawn around 2026-06-12):'' the admin island rides a bespoke 370-line twin of the pool's island stack (`admin-vm-core` — own spawn, own sync channel, own handshake with its own private timeout), duplicated again per substrate in the browser. Four copies of one hull. Every stack divergence found this week (the 15s/120s watchdog split) grew in this gap — the path off the common road accumulates silent breakage proportional to its specialness.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/life-support-asymmetry>>

!! The Life-Support Asymmetry

The field went to full uniformity and came back (kubeadm self-hosting deprecated and removed — a self-hosted control plane could not survive a reboot; bootkube retired; Talos's public reversal). The stable attractor, adopted here as law:

''Isomorphism of form, interface, and grants; asymmetry of life support.''

The thing that boots and restarts the admin island MUST NOT depend on the admin island living. The judge of admin's health sits //below// the substrate, reading evidence admin cannot fabricate or withhold — readiness reads local, one layer down.

''The genesis exception, named and bounded'' (every mature system keeps exactly this set: k8s static pods, Erlang `init`, the seL4 root task):

# a ''static, declarative genesis manifest'' read from local disk — data continuously derivable from the same source of truth, never a hand-maintained twin;
# a ''dumb loader'' that spawns the first island from it — small, frozen, no ongoing management;
# the ''first-grant seed'' — the first credential cannot come from the grant system;
# a ''liveness floor'' below the pool.

Everything else in the bespoke admin stack — handshake, sync ports, `ea`, the capability table, the verb surface — belongs to the shared hull. A genesis exception ages best when it shrinks toward ending (the seL4 root task destroys itself after distributing capabilities).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/migration>>

!! Migration — the pivot playbook (no flag day)

Incremental, witness-pointed, per the kubeadm-pivot and Chromium-servicification precedents:

# ''Interface isomorphism first:'' the admin island consumes the shared island stack (manifest, `ea`, sync, grants table) while keeping its bespoke spawner. Witness: existing suites green; admin reachable through the same protocol surface as any island. //First slice landed 2026-06-12: the admin ea-wait now rides the shared `awaitIslandMsg` watchdog (breath re-arm, stall budget, fault fast-reject) — the bespoke admin timer died; pool and admin share one watchdog mechanism.//
# ''Derive genesis from the common emitter:'' the admin genesis manifest gets produced by the same code path that emits ordinary island manifests; diff against the hand-rolled one — the fixed-point witness (stage2 ≡ stage3).
# ''Collapse the substrate twins:'' one stack + a substrate adapter (the `ListeningWSServerAdapter` precedent). The browser inherits, never re-implements. //Genesis intake collapsed 2026-06-12: validate→import→verify + CID reconcile live once in mesh `genesis-intake`, beside the emitter; the twins kept only byte sources, and the drift the gap had already grown (divergent record shape + authority string) died with it.//
# ''Delete the bespoke lines last.'' What remains special = the genesis manifest + loader + first-grant seed + liveness floor — small, frozen, named.

A mirror-pod gesture MAY bridge observability early: the statically-loaded admin island registers a passive twin of itself in the pool's slot space, so uniform tooling sees it before life support migrates anything.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/hoike-life-support>>

!! Hoike — the kept dispute

<<~ hoike #full-uniformity held="isomorphism of form, interface, and grants; asymmetry of life support — the genesis layer stays below the substrate (house, on three-system field evidence; operator to ratify)">>
q: does the one-hull law extend to admin's LIFE SUPPORT — the pool managing admin's own boot and restart?
<<~ kue voice=Mischief-Muse key="a vessel demonstrates admin-island death and restart with life support riding the pool itself, surviving a full vessel reboot">>
the purest reading makes no exception at all: the pool mounts admin like any island, the mailbox parks admin's verbs like any island's, and the genesis loader reduces to one bootstrap meme the corpus itself carries. The field's retraction came from Kubernetes-shaped systems with network-dependent control planes — a local-first vessel whose substrate reads from disk may not share the failure mode that killed self-hosting there.
<<~/kue>>
<<~ saksi voice="Spirit [hull[Stranger]]" scope=deposition>>deposition quoted at handback, before dissolution: "Full self-hosting was tried at scale and retracted — kubeadm deprecation, bootkube retirement, Talos reversal. The stable attractor is isomorphism of form and interface, asymmetry of life support... Don't let the isomorphism law accidentally make the pool's view of admin's liveness route through admin."<<~/saksi>>
re-entry: the kue key; or the migration's step 4 boundary, where the residue gets measured against the Muse's reading
<<~/hoike>>

<<~/ahu>>

